<title>INDIA: India's IDBI Bank cuts prime rate to 15.5 percent.</title>
<headline>India's IDBI Bank cuts prime rate to 15.5 percent.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's privately-run IDBI Bank will cut its prime lending rate to 15.5 percent annually from 16.5 percent from May 1, a bank official said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The revised rate will be exclusive of interest tax, he said.</p>
<p>The rate cut follows measures announced by the Reserve Bank of India to reduce deposit rates in its monetary policy for the first half of financial year 1997/98 (April-March), released on April 15.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
